WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.820
Mark: HELLO EVERYBODY, WE'RE BACK!

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:01.780
We're gonna play more Rust.

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.520
My name is Markiplier, that's Bob.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.260
Mark: Hey!

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.280
*THAT ZOOM*Bob: Oh, hey

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:05.780
Mark: Okay.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.880
Mark: Alright, let's GOOOO!

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.880
Mark: Alright, y-you lead the way this time,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.380
Mark: I - I led the way last time.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.460
Bob: I think we should go to that town that I had seen.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.460
Mark: Oh, you saw another walled-in town over there?

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.100
Bob: Yeah.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.220
Mark: It's probably irradiated, but I think that's gonna be okay.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.400
Bob: There's also these boxes that I'm interested in getting.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.320
Mark: Oh, yeah, that's true.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.660
Mark: Ooo there's another crate over here.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.100
Bob: That one had a spring.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.300
Mark: This one has a can of tuna and an apple.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:26.900
Bob: Neat.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.220
Bob: We need that food stuff, 'cause I don't know how really to get food in this game.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.960
Mark: Yeah you- well, I mean, you just gotta scavenge until you can find a way to farm it I think.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.800
Bob: Yeah, except there's no efficient way to scavenge it!

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.620
Mark: Yeah that's true too.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:43.360
Bob: I was desperately searching for food the whole time when we were looking for each other and I found, like, an apple and a can of tuna.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.060
Mark: Well-
Bob: In total.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.440
Mark: Ideally, you find more rocks and get more wood,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:53.580
and then you're able to hunt the deer and that should probably keep you fed for a long time, right?

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.460
Bob: Yeah i still dont know what rocks look like, so...

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.960
Mark: Well, I mean, I will show you if we ever come across it.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.060
Mark: But I have not come across one.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.360
Mark: I don't think-
Bob: You think with all those rocks we had seen, that those might have had been rocks?

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.600
Mark: Y- No
Bob: But they weren-

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.420
*f^ck up noises* Mark: WaaHey! Don't go in there!

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.760
Bob: Oh Jesus Cripes! (Cripes Bob?)
Mark: Ho!

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.380
Mark: Woah, I'm just gonna get some wood for a bit.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.940
Mark: Jeez, well, my health is going down. That's great.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.220
Bob: How much did you get? I got 20 Radiation Poisoning.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:23.120
Mark: I got a good 18 or so. I tried to warn you, but then it's just like you were barreling in there!

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.140
Bob: Well I was sprinting in behind you and

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.200
Bob: all you said before I got there was "HAOoo! WOW!"
Mark: *laughs*

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.440
Mark: That could've been anything.
Bob: And I was like, "Oh, that could be good or bad, I don't know."

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.060
Mark: *laughs* Could've been a whole depository of FOOD and GUNS and ammo and armor! (You keep dreaming Mark)

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.220
Bob: Could even be a boat, who fucking knows?
Mark: *laughs*

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:40.280
Mark: I mean, hey, if I found a boat, I'd be pretty excited about it.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.700
*turns into obnoxious cartoon character* Bob: "Waho! Woah ho! Waao!"
Mark: *laughs*

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.160
Happy Mark: "Boats! Boats! Boats!"

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.360
disappointed Mark: Uhp, my tree disappeared.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.280
Bob: I'm gonna make a bow. How much do you need? You need cloth for a bow.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.800
Mark: Mmhm
Bob: Fuck.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.480
Mark: Where is the more-?
Bob: I've got lots of WOOD!

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.220
Bob: Like a serious boner for wood!

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:59.900
Mark: It used to be that you could just chop rocks and get stone out of it. Why is it so hard to get stone these days?

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.860
Mark: This stone? Nope, that not the right rock.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.260
Bob: Why am I double-crafting hammer? I just want one hammer.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.220
Mark: Oh yeah, what does hammer do?

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.160
Bob: Can't I just have one hammer?

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.400
Bob: I assume- *breathes in* WAIT! I remember!
Mark: Oh?!

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:10.900
Mark: OHH!

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.220
Bob: We're fucking dumb!
Mark: What?

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.940
Bob: You HAMMER rocks to get ROCKS! (or so you thought you're close)

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.880
Mark: Oh, you can't ROCK to get ROCK? (NOPE)

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.920
Mark: You can't ROCK rock to get ROCK?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.320
Bob: But you can HAMMER rocks to get ROCKS! (He thinks he's got it)

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.160
Mark: Can you? (not at all)
Bob: Nope, not these ones.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.140
Mark: *laughs*
Bob: I'm not sure what the hammer's for. (nothing)

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.000
Mark: Yeah, that's not how.
Bob: Can we get SOME explanation on the hammer?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.840
Mark: Nah nah nah.
Bob: The hammer used to upgrade building materials *quietly* and i hit the thing

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.000
Bob: *pause* *in the "You've Got Mail" voice* right click for the options.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:33.680
*intense ZOOM* Bob: Fuck.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:34.240
Mark: Ha ha.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.040
Bob: Whatever, I have a hammer now, motherfucker!

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.700
Mark: Alright, I'm gonna see how much radiation is in this town... Not much!

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:40.420
Mark: Nothing yet! *le gasp*

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:40.940
 

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.740
Bob: Alright, good job Bob!

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.460
Mark [high pitched]: Good job Bob, good job!

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.680
Bob: Didn't there used to be like, zombies or something in this game?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.900
Mark: Hang on, wait, I found a door. I'm gonna rock my way through it.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.640
Bob: Is that you, slamming around the door?
Mark: No, it looks like someone BUILT a door here.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.580
Bob: I'm gonna-
Mark: I'm gonna rock my way in!

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.120
Bob: I'm over to your left, crossing very slowly and cautiously.
Mark: Yeah, okay.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:02.720
Mark: Woohp uhp!

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.700
Bob: If anything goes wrong, I'll just start yelling.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.240
Mark: Oh this- Oh, there's- SURPRISE!

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.580
Mark: There was another DOOR behind the door!
Bob: Oh neat!

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:14.440
Mark: Yeah, I don't know how that worked, but okay. Looks like this guy built multiple doors here, didn't want anyone getting in.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.180
Mark: Okay! There was another DOOR behind that DOOR! Why are there so many doors stacked on each other here?

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.380
Bob: There's a Recycler, and a Crafting- There's a Repair Bench in here.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.920
Mark: Ooo! That sounds good!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.700
Bob: But I don't have anything that's worth repairing!

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:26.880
*both giggle*

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.920
Mark: FUCKING! It's just nonstop doors upon doors here!

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:30.760
Mark: This is fucking bullshit.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.460
Bob: Did you try OPENING them?

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.900
Mark: No, it's like wooden- It's just boarded up, that's all it is.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.720
Bob: Oh okay.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.460
Bob: Well-
Mark: I'm gonna- My rock is gonna disappear.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.160
Mark: My hammer didn't do anything. GODDAMMIT! It's anothe-

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.120
Mark: It's ENDLESS doors here! This is NOT gonna work.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.580
Bob: *giggles*
Mark: Fuckin' god damn it.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.800
Bob: It's fuckin' door-pocalypse up in there!
Mark: Fuckin' god damn it.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.560
Bob: Well this is like spooky and cool, but I'm not getting SHIT.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.860
Mark: Yeah...
Bob: I'm not getting any loot at all.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.560
Mark: Yeah, I see you way over there.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.500
Mark: Yeah, there's nothing over here. Whoops.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.400
Bob: Oh, there's a Can in here that I can bash open.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.100
Bob: You hear that action?
Mark: Yeah.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.340
Bob: That's some sweet action.
Mark: That's pretty sweet bashin', dude.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.260
Bob: Had literally nothing in it? Are you shitting me?

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.040
Mark: *groan*
Bob: Alright, well.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.600
Mark: Alright, I'm gonna- I'm gonna...

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.960
Bob: Do we need to explore down into this ravine?
Mark: Oh, shit.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.540
Mark: You can throw your rock. Did you know that?

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.800
Bob: OH! There's RADIATION in there!

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.600
Mark: Wooh!
Bob: Ah, fucks sake, I have 68 Radiation Poisoning!

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.820
Bob: I'm just gonna straight up die now.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.940
Mark: That sounds like death.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.100
Mark: Okay! Meet you back at the sleeping bags, buddy!

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.660
Bob: It's a race! I wonder who will win!
Mark: *giggles*

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.380
Bob: Well whatever, if I'm already gonna fucking die, fuck it, I'm going in here.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.820
Mark: Alright, good luck!

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.540
Bob: I died.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.900
Mark: Yay! Okay, I see you back in 'nother life.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.220
Bob: Oh, thank god I'm alive again!

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.780
Bob [sarcastic]: Woohoo!

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.000
Mark: We should play Second Life, is what we should play.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.120
Bob: THAT was fruitful!

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.520
Bob: Second Life? What is that?

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.620
Mark: You never heard of- You've heard of Second Life.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.600
Bob: No, of course not. I haven't heard of that.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.020
Mark [softly]: Everyone's heard of Second Life!
Bob: That's presumptuous.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.720
Mark:  Every One's heard of Second Life.
Bob: ........

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.300
Bob: That's still presumptuous, just 'cause you say it differently doesn't-

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.620
Mark [softly growling]: Ev- Everyone's heard of Second Life, man.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.300
Bob: ...no...

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.120
Mark [softly]: Dude.
Bob: Well now it just sounds like my music is broken.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.320
Bob: It's just like, I don't think it's supposed to be like this.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.040
Mark: Where'd you go? Where'd you go?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.400
Bob: I'm at the BabSacks.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.360
Mark: Ok. Oh THERE, I see.
Bob: I'm to your left on the hill.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.920
Mark: Okay, let's go a different way, because I know there are a lot of rocks over this way.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.660
Mark: I found 'em on the way here, and then it was just like a desolate wasteland.
Bob: Alright.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.580
Bob: Let's do that shit.
Mark: And I know that we need rocks.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.480
Bob: I'm gonna scavenge THIS though, before we go.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.260
Mark: Ok, you do that.
Bob: I got some water AND some food!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.020
Mark: Nice... God, you're so good at this game.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.140
Bob: You're the hunter, but I'm the gatherer!

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.780
Mark [softly]: Nice, nice man!

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.640
Bob: With my deep, deep voice.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.040
Mark: With your, sweet baps!

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.060
Bob: *giggles* Do you like the way my baps jiggle when I run?

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.300
Mark: Yeah, yeah man.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.020
Mark: Yeah I swear over- Where'd you go?
Bob: I'm right here

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:47.180
Mark: Ok. Over this wayyyy, there's fuckin', hemp and stuff.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.440
Bob: It's just gonna be rocks-a-plenty, huh?

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:56.620
Mark: NO! Maybe, I don't know! I can't believe we're STRUGGLING! To get FUCKING ROCKS!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:02.040
Bob: Yeah, I mean I've seen lots of other random crap so far, but I haven't actually collected a rock.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.880
Mark: I swear... 
Bob: And there are SO MANY ROOOOCKS!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.900
Mark: I swear... Wait, here! Right here! Right here!

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.500
Bob: Oh, hey! It's a stone.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.620
Mark: It's a STOOONE. You can tell how its different than all the other rocks!

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:19.320
Bob: So the problem is that I don't want rocks, I want STONE!

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.540
Mark: TRUE!

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.820
Bob: I was had looking for the wrong THING.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.480
Mark: RIGHT

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.680
Mark: If you uh, had-ta-had-ta known that

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.120
Mark: you would've gotten it right.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.180
Bob: I would have had do that MUCH sooner

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.500
Mark: But NOW I have... problem, 'cause my fuckin'

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.540
Mark: bow disappeared

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.260
Mark [mumbled]: so I gotta make another one

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.060
Bob: (laughing) Just standin' there with a dead-eye stare

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.020
Bob: right through me

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:40.860
Mark: *laughs heartily*

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.920
Mark: He's walkin' up slowly with a rock like

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:44.860
Mark: "I'm gonna bash your face in,"

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.440
Mark: (Quietly suffocating) "Aye, fucking, goddamn it"

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.160
Bob: I think it'd be really funny, just as like an April Fool's

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.200
Bob: joke or something

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.400
Bob: If the dev's put it so that whenever anyone tried

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.580
Bob: to use the in-game voice chat, they would

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.180
Bob: they would push the push-to-talk and then it was just like

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.100
Bob: *walrus mating noises*

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.620
Mark: Woah, what the fuck is Sulfur Ore?

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:03.580
Mark: I just got that

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.420
Bob: Its stiiinky pee-yew!

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.520
Mark: *groans*
Bob: *snickers*

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:07.120
Mark: SO, apparently this--

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.580
Bob:-- Told you I was savin' that good stuff for this.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.260
Mark: Yeah this is good,

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.100
Mark: also i'm about to die.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:11.600
Mark: I'm low on--

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.240
Mark: foo-
Bob: I got food and water, ya need stuff?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.720
Mark: Uh, nah, you can hold onto that, I'm going tooo

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.940
Mark: I'm gonna dooo, I'M gonna, try to HUNT!

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.060
Bob: Just-just wham that shit with your rock

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.480
Bob: Just who- "who fuckin' cares"

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:26.540
Mark: Yeah man, why wouldn't I?

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.160
Mark: Just tryin' to see if it'll work, man.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.640
Mark: ALRIGHT, we should-we should OK

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.820
Mark: WE need to come up with a unified goal that's...

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.820
Mark: besides just not dying
Bob: I'm just running around...

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:37.360
Bob: ..near you. I mean, "Not dying" I  feel like is pretty ambitious as it is.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:40.000
Mark: True, very true. But we need like a long term-
Bob: You mean it would be easier...

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.560
Bob: ...not to die if we were more specific?
Mark: Yeah!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.320
Mark: Hey, wait, there's another town over here.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.680
Bob [sarcasm]: Yeah, that was really helpful last time we found a town.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:47.840
Mark: Well, I mean, it could be something.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.620
Bob: This time it's bound to be more gooder.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:50.340
Mark: I mean-

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.580
Bob: These rock formations are fucking amazing.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:53.440
Mark: Yeah.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.640
Bob: I gotta say, I wish I had surreal rock formations near me.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.600
Mark: Yeah, not bad.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.920
Mark: Uhh apparently I'm starving now, but my health isn't going down,

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:01.680
Mark: so I think I'm okay.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.760
Bob: I got food, man, I got extra food.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.580
Mark: Yeah, but I've only got 30 food.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.780
Mark: Or, I've got 30 food, so it should-

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.260
Mark: It should might last me.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.940
Bob: I know you're trying to lose weight, Mark. It's the new year and everything,

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:12.840
Bob: But starving yourself isn't the way.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.980
Mark: Nah man, I got it all under control, just, don't worry about it.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.540
Bob: You gotta do it responsibly.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.620
Mark: No, I got it, don't worry about it.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.600
Bob: No... You've been at the gym, like 8 hours a day.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.200
Bob: You haven't seen the kids all week.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.500
